    "result_text": "Build succeeds and all tests pass (`Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned the identity key with low structural impact by centralizing the logic in one small new class and having existing helpers delegate to it \u2014 the large classes (the controller and the `Owner` entity) were left untouched.\n\n**Files changed (5):**\n\n1. **`model/IdentityKeys.java`** (new) \u2014 the single source of truth: `of(Owner)` computes `SHA-256` hex over `normalizedTelephone + '|' + lowerEmail + '|' + soundex(lastName)`, plus a standard American `soundex(...)`. Small, cohesive, near-zero surrounding complexity.\n\n2. **`rest/controller/v1/Identities.java`** \u2014 `identityKey(...)` now delegates to `IdentityKeys.of(...)`; `isDuplicate` (the 409 check) is unchanged, so it automatically uses the new key. The controller's `addOwner` still filters out deleted owners and Bean Validation still applies the email-domain blocklist first \u2014 both untouched.\n\n3. **`rest/controller/v1/PossibleDuplicates.java`** \u2014 `softMatch` now triggers when the **identityKeys differ** but **soundex(lastName) matches** and **postcode matches** (so same surname+postcode with a different telephone becomes a soft match, not a 409).\n\n4. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `identityKey` property to the Owner schema (generates the DTO field).\n\n5. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 one `@Mapping` expression populating `identityKey` from `IdentityKeys.of(owner)` (added to the `@Mapper(imports=...)` list).\n\nThe separate household-duplicate 409 (`Households.isDuplicate`) was already not wired into the controller, so no removal was needed \u2014 duplicate detection is now solely the identity key.",
